season two of the mandalorian was an  easter egg field extravaganza  one that had many star wars fans leaping  for joy from the return of boba fett to  the live-action debut of clone wars  favourites such as bokotan  and ahsoka tano the second season of the  mandalorian somehow cleared the high  bar set by the first but if you ask many  fans about the biggest surprise moment  the second season had to offer  they will probably mention a certain  cloaked jedi who makes an appearance in  the finale  in chapter 16 the rescue the mandalorian  and his allies have pitted against the  legion of dark troopers  and or hope looks lost until a young  luke skywalker arrives on the scene  brings down the evil droids and takes  grogu off for some special jedi training  it was easily the series biggest moment  thus far with skywalker's youthful  appearance coming down to some unique  technology and a little collaboration  with mark hamill  the star wars legend who is also a  self-professed fan of the series  it's very much in the spirit of what  george wanted uh originally  and uh i just thought it was  superb still although many fans loved  this moment others were less impressed  mostly by the execution of skywalker's  dating process  either way you're about to learn more  about the technology that went into this  cameo moment  thanks to an upcoming disney plus  special centered around it  mandalorian fans may have already tuned  into the documentary series disney  gallery the mandalorian  which offers a behind the scenes look at  individual episodes of the show  and provides crucial information about  how each individual story  and the series as a whole came to life  now that season 2 has run its course  most fans assume that the mandalorians  disney gallery series was unlikely to  return until the main show's third  season  those same people might be surprised to  learn that the house of mouse is  bringing back its popular  behind-the-scenes star q series  well ahead of schedule with a fresh  episode set to hit disney plus in august  disney plus will premiere the special  episode of disney gallery on august 25th  2021 which focuses on the return of luke  skywalker and the mandalorian season 2  finale  among other things the episode will  reveal more about the type of technology  used to resurrect luke in his classic  return of the jedi look  as well as examine the collaborative  process with mark hamill that proved  essential to making luke's appearance as  realistic as possible  so if you were one of the many star wars  fans who got a little teary eyed at the  return of everyone's favorite jedi  master then this new episode of disney  gallery will be right up your alley  but what can we actually expect to learn  from it well aside from knowing that  actor max lloyd jones was responsible  for the bodywork of young luke  there's precious little anyone does know  about the technical and collaborative  work that went into luke's return  it's possible to make a reasonable guess  how it all works considering similar  technology has been used in previous  star wars movies  and elsewhere in hollywood but nothing  is certain here  outside of the production nobody's even  sure how much involvement hamill even  had in the process  but while many fans will be thrilled to  get some answers to those questions  others might be less than thrilled to  return to the mandalorian season 2  finale  indeed while the moment of luke's  triumph from return garnered much praise  from many  some would have preferred that disney  recast a role instead of using the aging  technology  online star wars fans even had a  consensus candidate to fill young  skywalker's jedi boots  mcu mainstay sebastian stan twitter user  at djson81  summed up the most emphatic faction of  the fandom swords  after the mandalorian season 2 finale  aired tweeting  jesus christ just use sebastian stan for  luke  rather than this janky ps3 cutscene  looking version we got  of course it'll be interesting to hear  whether anybody ever considered  recasting luke for his special  appearance in the mandalorian  or whether it was the aging tech all the  way for john favreau and company  whether they did or not though we're  bound to know for certain when the  newest episode of disney gallery hits  disney plus  this august check out one of our newest  videos right here plus  even more looper videos about the  mandalorian are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

